            0.126,
            0.083,
            0.743,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": "5. Manya is blindfolded. She is given two unknown solutions to test and determine whether they are acidic or basic. Which indicator should Manya use to test the solutions and why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.141,
            0.743,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "6. Could you suggest various materials which can be used for writing the message on the white sheet of paper (given at the beginning of the chapter) and what could be in the spray bottle? Make a table of various possible combinations and the colour of the writing obtained."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.235,
            0.742,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": "7. Grape juice was mixed with red rose extract; the mixture got a tint of red colour. What will happen if baking soda is added to this mixture? Justify your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.293,
            0.743,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "8. Keerthi wrote a secret message to her grandmother on her birthday using orange juice. Can you assist her grandmother in revealing the message? Which indicator would you use to make it visible?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.369,
            0.742,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "9. How can natural indicators be prepared? Explain by giving an example."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.408,
            0.743,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "10. Three liquids are given to you. One is vinegar, another is a baking soda solution, and the third is a sugar solution. Can you identify them only using turmeric paper? Explain."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.466,
            0.744,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "11. The extract of red rose turns the liquid X to green. What will the nature of liquid X be? What will happen when excess of amla juice is added to liquid X?"
